    "done_when": "tests/test_idle_producer_backs_off.py, in a temporary RECKON_HOME with no live run pointer, shows the producer's recorded poll_interval_seconds doubling on each idle poll from its base interval to the 30 s cap, and returning to the base on the first poll that sees a live run (a pointer for the project whose run is not terminal). It also shows that no sleep outlasts the lease's remaining time, so with RECKON_PRODUCER_LEASE_SECONDS=3 the backed-off producer still exits within one second of the lapse. The interval is written through the existing update_watch_registration (reckon/crew/runs.py is held by another session and is not edited); the lease is in watch_ticker since merge 320061aff and the unlinked-seat recreation since merge 149783489. The declared negative control is executed and logged: with the doubling removed, the interval stays at base and the test fails. Base and head arms of tests/test_producer_holds_a_lease.py, tests/test_producer_registration_survives_unlink.py and tests/test_producer_*.py show zero added failures.",
